---
// A terminal-owned session, watched live and read-only.
import Frame from "../Frame.astro";
import Icon from "../Icon.astro";
import ContextRing from "../ContextRing.astro";
---
<Frame path="demo-app" class="m-frame" caption="A session a terminal owns, streaming live in Sova with a TUI chip in its head. Its composer is disabled and reads: Read only while this session is open in the TUI.">
  <div class="m-session">
    <header class="m-head">
      <span class="m-head-title">Flaky upload test</span>
      <span class="chip chip-static">TUI</span>
      <span class="m-head-end m-mono m-muted"><ContextRing pct={58} tone="warn" />116k / 200k · 58%</span>
    </header>
    <div class="m-thread">
      <div class="m-msg-user">upload/client.test.ts fails about 1 run in 10. Find out why.</div>
      <div class="m-tool">
        <div class="m-tool-sum"><Icon name="chevron-down" size={12} /><span class="m-tool-name">bash</span><span class="m-tool-arg">for i in $(seq 20); do pnpm test client; done</span><span class="m-del">2 failed</span></div>
        <div class="m-tool-body">✗ resumes after a dropped connection{"\n"}  expected 3 chunks, received 2</div>
      </div>
      <p class="m-msg">The test's fake server closes the socket on a timer, and the timer races the second chunk. Pinning the clock should make it deterministic.</p>
      <div class="m-tool"><div class="m-tool-sum"><span class="live-dot"></span><span class="m-tool-name">edit</span><span class="m-tool-arg">test/upload/client.test.ts</span></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="m-composer m-composer-off">
      <div class="m-composer-reason"><Icon name="terminal" size={14} />Read only while this session is open in the TUI.</div>
      <div class="m-composer-row">
        <span class="m-input">&nbsp;</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Frame>
